# Description
In this challenge, you had to overflow the heap that was given in the challenge. You had to connect to the instance using 
the given powershell command:
nc tethys.picoctf.net 61988

# Solution
The solution to this challenge required me to look into the given source code. The source code listed that the allocated memory
for input_data was 64 so the buffer I wrote was 32 characters long. This broke the heap printing the flag
flag: picoCTF{my_first_heap_overflow_1ad0e1a6}
